		<!-- ===== M3.6 Oleada 10: lint baseline on demand =====
		     Activate with `-Plint-report`. Binds Checkstyle to the `verify`
		     phase with failOnViolation=false so the build does not break
		     while the baseline is being measured. Reports land under
		     <module>/target/checkstyle-result.xml. The default build
		     (without this profile) does *not* run any lint tool.

		     Spotless, PMD and SpotBugs are declared in <pluginManagement>
		     but intentionally NOT bound here. Each has a different reason
		     and a different ad-hoc invocation path:

		     - Spotless `check` fails by design on any deviation (no
		       warn-only mode), and the tree mixes CRLF/LF line endings +
		       import orderings. Ad-hoc: `mvn spotless:check` (report) /
		       `mvn spotless:apply` (rewrite).

		     - PMD 7.14 has incomplete JDK 21+ compatibility: it cannot
		       parse newer JDK core class files (`ClassStub:java/lang/String`
		       fails) and triggers StackOverflowError in symbol resolution
		       on this codebase under JDK 26. Ad-hoc on a JDK 21 host:
		       `mvn pmd:pmd`. Re-binding deferred until PMD 7.x stabilizes
		       JDK 21+ support.

		     - SpotBugs 4.9.x relies on ASM bytecode parsing that does not
		       yet support JDK 26 class file format. On a JDK 21 host it
		       works correctly; on JDK 26 (the current dev machine) it
		       errors on `java/lang/Object` and exits 1, breaking the
		       build. Ad-hoc on a JDK 21 host: `mvn spotbugs:spotbugs`.
		       Re-binding deferred until SpotBugs upgrades ASM to support
		       JDK 26 or until CI standardizes on JDK 21.

		     Checkstyle parses source code (not bytecode), so it is JDK-
		     version-agnostic and stays as the always-on gate. -->
		<profile>
			<id>lint-report</id>
			<build>
				<plugins>
					<plugin>
						<groupId>org.apache.maven.plugins</groupId>
						<artifactId>maven-checkstyle-plugin</artifactId>
						<executions>
							<execution>
								<id>checkstyle-report</id>
								<phase>verify</phase>
								<goals>
									<goal>check</goal>
								</goals>
							</execution>
						</executions>
					</plugin>
				</plugins>
			</build>
		</profile>

